in a stunning reversal of Fortune  Elizabeth Holmes wants a Silicon Valley  Superstar was sentenced to more than 11  years in prison on Friday she was  convicted on fraud and conspiracy  charges earlier this year Holmes carried  out a massive scheme to deceive the  investors who put up nearly a billion  dollars in her biotech company theranos  Anna Werner was in the courtroom  Elizabeth Holmes holding hands with  family entered federal court in San Jose  California expressionless but just a few  hours later before her sentencing stood  in front of the judge weeping and told  him I stand before you taking  responsibility for theranos I loved  theranos it was my life's work she said  I am devastated by my failings every day  I have felt deep pain for what people  went through because I failed them judge  Edward Davila then sentenced her to 135  months over 11 years in federal prison  testing more accessible it was a  stunning fall for 38 year old homes who  had once seemed the Golden Girl of  Silicon Valley a Stanford University  Dropout who rocketed onto magazine  covers by launching her own blood  testing company in 2003 when she was  just 19 years old she then wowed  unsuspecting investors who poured  millions of dollars into what was  supposed to be a Cutting Edge company  earlier this year a jury convicted  Holmes on four counts of conspiracy and  fraud for misleading those investors  while acquitting her on another four  counts of defrauding patients the panel  was unable to reach a decision on the  remaining three charges  Holmes's attorneys had argued for a  sentence of 18 months of confinement at  home where homes now pregnant with her  second child could care for her toddler  and her new baby but after the judge  handed down the sentence prosecutors  said in a press release that it reflects  the audacity of her massive fraud and  the Staggering damage she caused the  judge ordered Holmes to turn herself in  in April next year for CBS Saturday  morning Anna Werner San Jose California
 

